 ## Background
-The concept of pre-integration for volume rendering was introduced by Levoy and Whitted in 1985 [S1]. The method was further developed and popularized for real-time rendering on early graphics hardware, such as the Silicon Graphics VGX and NVidia GeForce3, demonstrating performance improvements of 1-4 frames per second for $256^3$ volumes [S1]. The quadratic approximation for exponential blending was proposed to facilitate hardware acceleration using Gouraud shading [S1].
